{"id": "section-body-06464", "title": "Pediatric Hydrocephalus", "chapterId": "chapter-eight", "tocLevel": 4, "tocPath": ["APPROACH TO PATIENTS WITH EMERGENCY CONDITIONS", "NERVOUS SYSTEM DISEASE CONDITIONS", "Congenital Pediatric Nervous System Diseases", "Pediatric Hydrocephalus"], "blocks": [{"id": "body-06464", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Pediatric Hydrocephalus", "runs": [{"text": "Pediatric"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Hydrocephalus"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 2, "numberingId": "1659"}}, {"id": "body-06465", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Pediatric hydrocephalus (HDC) is a common surgically correctable neurological problem in children with estimated incidence of 1 in every 500 children. HDC can result from various congenital and acquired causes including aqueductal stenosis, Chiari malformations, intraventricular hemorrhage, trauma, tumors, and infection. There are effective surgical interventions that can preserve and improve quality of life in patients with HDC.", "runs": [{"text": "Pediatric"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "hydrocephalus"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(HDC)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "common"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "surgically"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "correctable"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "neurological"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "problem"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "children"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "estimated"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "incidence of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "1"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "every"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "500"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "children."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "HDC"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "can"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "result"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "from"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "various"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "congenital"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "acquired"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "causes"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "including"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "aqueductal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "stenosis,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Chiari malformations,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "intraventricular"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "hemorrhage,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "trauma,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "tumors,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "infection."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "There"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "are"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "effective"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "surgical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "interventions"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "that"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "can preserve and improve quality of life in patients with HDC."}]}, {"id": "body-06467", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Clinical Presentation", "runs": [{"text": "Clinical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Presentation"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-06468", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Abnormal increase in head size, Seizure, Delayed/regressed developmental milestones, Headache and impaired vision", "runs": [{"text": "Abnormal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "increase"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "head"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "size,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Seizure,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Delayed/regressed"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "developmental"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "milestones,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Headache"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "impaired"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "vision"}]}, {"id": "body-06470", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Investigations", "runs": [{"text": "Investigations"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-06471", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Cranial Ultrasound", "runs": [{"text": "Cranial"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Ultrasound"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1640"}}, {"id": "body-06472", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Non contrast head CT scan", "runs": [{"text": "Non"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "contrast"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "head"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "CT"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "scan"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1640"}}, {"id": "body-06473", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "MRI brain scan", "runs": [{"text": "MRI"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "brain"}, {"text": " scan"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1640"}}, {"id": "body-06475", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Surgical Management:", "runs": [{"text": "Surgical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Management:"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-06476", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Endoscopic third ventriculostomy with choroid plexus coagulation (ETV+CPC) as first line option in cases with clear obstruction to CSF flow.", "runs": [{"text": "Endoscopic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "third"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "ventriculostomy"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "choroid"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "plexus"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "coagulation"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(ETV+CPC)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "as"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "first"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "line"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "option"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "cases"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "clear obstruction to CSF flow."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1640"}}, {"id": "body-06477", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Insertion of ventriculoperitoneal shunt (VP shunt) where ETV+CPC is not available, has failed, or is contraindicated. Other alternative CSF shunts include ventriculoarterial (VA) or ventriculopleural shunts, as well as ventriculo- subgaleal shunting.", "runs": [{"text": "Insertion"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "ventriculoperitoneal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "shunt"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(VP"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "shunt)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "where"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "ETV+CPC"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "not"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "available,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "has"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "failed,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "contraindicated. Other alternative CSF shunts include ventriculoarterial (VA) or ventriculopleural shunts, as well as ventriculo- subgaleal shunting."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1640"}}, {"id": "body-06479", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Non-Pharmacological Management", "runs": [{"text": "Non-Pharmacological"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Management"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-06480", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Physiotherapy", "runs": [{"text": "Physiotherapy"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1640"}}, {"id": "body-06481", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Educational therapy", "runs": [{"text": "Educational"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "therapy"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1640"}}, {"id": "body-06482", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Screening for other congenital anomaly", "runs": [{"text": "Screening"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "for"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "other"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "congenital"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "anomaly"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1640"}}, {"id": "body-06484", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Pharmacological Management", "runs": [{"text": "Pharmacological"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Management"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-06485", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Management of associated seizures:", "runs": [{"text": "Management"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "associated"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "seizures:"}]}, {"id": "body-06487", "type": "paragraph", "style": "Bod